# ── Reiwa OS environment ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app runs on PostgreSQL (Supabase in production). All variables below are
# required at runtime.

# Privileged Postgres connection — on Supabase use the TRANSACTION POOLER URL
# (aws-…pooler.supabase.com:6543, user postgres.<project-ref>). Used for
# migrations, seeding, staff profile lookup; per-request queries run inside it
# under `set local role authenticated` + request.jwt.claims (RLS enforced).
DATABASE_URL=

# Supabase project + API keys. The publishable key is safe for the browser;
# the SECRET key is server-only and used exclusively for the Auth Admin API
# (src/lib/auth/admin.ts) — deliberately separate from DATABASE_URL access.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# ── Local development without a hosted Supabase project ─────────────────────
# 1. Run a local Postgres and point DATABASE_URL at it (the migration runner
#    applies supabase/local/auth_shim.sql automatically on plain Postgres).
# 2. Run the GoTrue-compatible stub:  node scripts/dev-auth-stub.mjs
# 3. NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9999
#    NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=local-dev  (any non-empty value)
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=   # stub signing secret (defaults to the Supabase local default)

# ── Tests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Privileged connection used by tests to create throwaway databases.
# TEST_DATABASE_ADMIN_URL=postgres://postgres@127.0.0.1:55432/postgres
